  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a positive integer `n`. Identify whether `n` is divisible by the **sum** of the following two values:\n\n* The **digit sum** of `n` (the sum of its digits).\n* The **digit** **product** of `n` (the product of its digits).\n\nOutput `true` if `n` is divisible by this sum; otherwise, output `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** n = 99\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nSince 99 is divisible by the sum (9 + 9 = 18) plus product (9 \\* 9 = 81) of its digits (total 99), the output is true.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** n = 23\n\n**Output:** false\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nSince 23 is not divisible by the sum (2 + 3 = 5) plus product (2 \\* 3 = 6) of its digits (total 11), the output is false.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 106`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
